            <ArticleTitle>Multiple myeloma: managing a complex blood cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S18-28</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12968/bjon.2016.25.S18</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article gives a comprehensive overview of multiple myeloma (MM), a complex blood cancer involving overproduction of plasma cells. Although MM remains incurable, patients are living longer as a result of multiple treatment options. However, MM patients are also living with a higher symptom burden. The overall aims in managing MM are therefore to control disease progression, prolong survival and improve quality of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
